      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Base: music, dialogue or action\n\nOne shot per image over your track, in order. Load a track and your images, pick **mode** and press Run.\n\n- **mode**: *music* cuts whole bars from the downbeat after *start_at*, guided by the kick of **drums**; *dialogue* cuts in the pauses, guided by **voice**; *action* cuts between hits, guided by the track.\n- **Audio Separation** feeds **drums** and **voice** from your track, so switching mode is one click.\n- **duration**: how long the video runs from *start_at*. One image and 30 s gives one 30 s shot.\n- **Context windows**: each shot is sampled in overlapping ~5 s windows, so shots can run 30 s and more and keep their look. Bypass the node for the tightest sync on short shots.\n- **Anchor** (optional): to hold a hard style or a character across the cuts, connect a character or style sheet to *Reference to Video*'s second image slot and add *drawn in the art style of <Picture 2>* to the prompt. Not a full scene: H3 may animate the anchor instead of the shot's image.\n- **Timeline**: drag the yellow handles to set the range, double-click a shot to split it, right-click a cut to merge, *One shot* for a single long shot. Hover it for hints, **?** lists every control, **Analyse** shows the exact cuts without rendering.\n\n- **Trim Audio Duration**: the part of the track to use (start and length in seconds); *start_at* and *duration* count from the start of the trim.\n\n**This version: fast.** The pika LoRA, 8 steps, CFG 1. For hits that land harder, bypass the LoRA and use 30 steps and CFG 5: the negative is already zeroed before the guide.\n\nNodes: Syntax Timeline and the optional Syntax Preview Strip (the sync bar along the bottom; delete it to hide); everything else is core."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Base: music, dialogue or action\n\nOne shot per image over your track, in order. Load a track and your images, pick **mode** and press Run.\n\n- **mode**: *music* cuts whole bars from the downbeat after *start_at*, guided by the kick of **drums**; *dialogue* cuts in the pauses, guided by **voice**; *action* cuts between hits, guided by the track.\n- **Audio Separation** feeds **drums** and **voice** from your track, so switching mode is one click.\n- **duration**: how long the video runs from *start_at*. One image and 30 s gives one 30 s shot.\n- **Context windows**: each shot is sampled in overlapping ~5 s windows, so shots can run 30 s and more and keep their look. Bypass the node for the tightest sync on short shots.\n- **Anchor** (optional): to hold a hard style or a character across the cuts, connect a character or style sheet to *Reference to Video*'s second image slot and add *drawn in the art style of <Picture 2>* to the prompt. Not a full scene: H3 may animate the anchor instead of the shot's image.\n- **Timeline**: drag the yellow handles to set the range, double-click a shot to split it, right-click a cut to merge, *One shot* for a single long shot. Hover it for hints, **?** lists every control, **Analyse** shows the exact cuts without rendering.\n\n- **Trim Audio Duration**: the part of the track to use (start and length in seconds); *start_at* and *duration* count from the start of the trim.\n\n**This version: fast.** The pika LoRA, 8 steps, CFG 1. For hits that land harder, bypass the LoRA and use 30 steps and CFG 5: the negative is already zeroed before the guide.\n\nNodes: Syntax Timeline and the optional Syntax Preview Strip (the sync bar along the bottom; delete it to hide); everything else is core."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
